WEBVTT

00:00:07.238 --> 00:00:10.371
We need to make sure
our own string is safe.

00:00:10.415 --> 00:00:13.374
Uh, our string is safe.

00:00:13.418 --> 00:00:14.375
What?!

00:00:14.419 --> 00:00:15.855
Poppy, are-are you crazy?

00:00:15.899 --> 00:00:17.857
I thought it was a good idea
at the time.

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:21.382
I-I can't believe another queen
would use her power for evil.

00:00:21.426 --> 00:00:22.688
Okay. Change of plans.

00:00:22.732 --> 00:00:24.385
We need to get home
as fast as we can

00:00:24.429 --> 00:00:25.648
and get everyone in the bunker.

00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:27.476
Uh, no. Change of plans.

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:29.869
We have to stop Barb
from destroying all music.

00:00:29.913 --> 00:00:31.654
If we don't stop her, who will?

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:33.525
Poppy, you said this could be
handled with hugs.

00:00:33.569 --> 00:00:35.962
How are we gonna hug
our way out of this one?

00:00:36.006 --> 00:00:37.181
-It's okay, Biggie.
-Really?

00:00:37.224 --> 00:00:38.791
It's okay to be terrified?

00:00:38.835 --> 00:00:40.880
When am I gonna learn to stay
away from the cotton candy?!

00:00:40.924 --> 00:00:41.881
No.

00:00:41.925 --> 00:00:43.317
As your queen,

00:00:43.361 --> 00:00:46.146
I promise that I will
protect you, no matter what.

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.846
I... pinky promise.

00:00:49.889 --> 00:00:51.761
[gasps]

00:00:51.804 --> 00:00:56.374
Poppy, you know you can't
go back on a pinky promise.

00:00:56.417 --> 00:00:58.898
Never did, never will.

00:00:58.942 --> 00:01:02.206
♪

00:01:02.249 --> 00:01:03.990
-[electricity crackles]
-[magic jingling]

00:01:04.034 --> 00:01:06.253
[wind whooshing]

00:01:09.039 --> 00:01:10.910
[laughs]

00:01:10.954 --> 00:01:12.346
Farewell!

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:17.743
A pinky promise.

00:01:17.787 --> 00:01:19.223
Dang.

00:01:22.269 --> 00:01:24.054
Let it be so.

00:01:24.097 --> 00:01:26.622
And so it is.

00:01:26.665 --> 00:01:27.753
[groans]

00:01:27.797 --> 00:01:30.364
This just got real.

00:01:30.408 --> 00:01:32.149
POPPY: We have to get to
the Country Music Trolls

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.717
in Lonesome Flats
before Barb does.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.457
Will you come with us?

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:37.415
Oh, no.

00:01:37.458 --> 00:01:39.809
Someone has to rebuild.

00:01:39.852 --> 00:01:45.249
And Pennywhistle is
that woodwind for the job.

00:01:46.076 --> 00:01:47.686
[grunts]

00:01:54.171 --> 00:01:55.912
Good luck, little Pennywhistle.

00:01:56.956 --> 00:01:59.176
Goodbye, Poppy.

00:02:02.527 --> 00:02:03.702
[sighs]

00:02:04.573 --> 00:02:06.836
[whooping, excited shouting]

00:02:06.879 --> 00:02:09.578
[growling]

00:02:10.666 --> 00:02:12.798
Wait. Is that...

00:02:12.842 --> 00:02:14.017
-Debbie?
-Oh, what?

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:15.496
-Oh, that's a lot of glitter.
-BARB: No!

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.586
What did they do to you,
my hairy little baby?!

00:02:17.629 --> 00:02:18.804
Come here, come here,
come here.

00:02:18.848 --> 00:02:20.327
-Gnarly.
-What-what-what do you...

00:02:20.371 --> 00:02:22.155
-What is this?
-What, what...

00:02:22.199 --> 00:02:23.809
Pop Trolls?

00:02:23.853 --> 00:02:24.897
[clears throat]

00:02:24.941 --> 00:02:27.639
"Dear Barb,
can't wait to meet you.

00:02:27.683 --> 00:02:30.250
I have tons of
great party ideas."

00:02:30.294 --> 00:02:31.643
I like that.

00:02:31.687 --> 00:02:34.428
"Maybe you and I
can even be best friends."

00:02:34.472 --> 00:02:35.821
Best friends?

00:02:35.865 --> 00:02:37.867
Is she making fun of me?

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:39.825
No one says that.

00:02:39.869 --> 00:02:42.828
Friendship takes time and years
of mutual care and respect.

00:02:42.872 --> 00:02:44.700
You don't just become
best friends.

00:02:44.743 --> 00:02:48.660
Plus, everyone knows I already
have a ton of friends.

00:02:48.704 --> 00:02:49.792
Like Carol.

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:51.402
Right, Carol?

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:54.405
Okay, you're busy.
That's fine.

00:02:54.448 --> 00:02:55.406
Love you, Carol.

00:02:55.449 --> 00:02:57.713
[quiet crackling]

00:03:00.803 --> 00:03:03.544
POPPY [over speaker]:
♪ Trolls just wanna have fun.

00:03:03.588 --> 00:03:04.502
[growls]

00:03:04.545 --> 00:03:06.199
-Gnarly.
-[back-up alarm beeping]

00:03:06.243 --> 00:03:08.680
Pop music isn't even
real music!

00:03:08.724 --> 00:03:11.857
It's bland! It's repetitive!

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:14.033
The lyrics are empty!

00:03:14.077 --> 00:03:18.037
Worst of all, it crawls into
your head like an earworm!

00:03:18.081 --> 00:03:20.692
[chain saw buzzing]

00:03:20.736 --> 00:03:22.172
[sighs]

00:03:22.215 --> 00:03:24.391
You know, and you can't
get it out-- Uh, I'm tired now.

00:03:24.435 --> 00:03:27.133
[whoops] Hating things
takes a lot of energy.

00:03:27.177 --> 00:03:29.701
♪ Trolls just wanna have fun

00:03:29.745 --> 00:03:31.355
-♪ Trolls just wanna...
-No. No.

00:03:31.398 --> 00:03:32.791
Look what their music
just did to Dad.

00:03:32.835 --> 00:03:34.227
-Daddy? Come back.
-[slurping]

00:03:34.271 --> 00:03:35.664
Come back to me, Daddy.

00:03:36.839 --> 00:03:38.579
Nice hair, dude.

00:03:38.623 --> 00:03:40.581
No one does this to Dad.

00:03:40.625 --> 00:03:42.888
And no one makes fun
of Queen Barb.

00:03:42.932 --> 00:03:43.759
[humming]

00:03:43.802 --> 00:03:46.457
Ah! I need that Pop string.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.764
And I know who's gonna help me.

00:03:48.807 --> 00:03:52.332
The most feared bounty hunters
in all of Trolldom.

00:03:52.376 --> 00:03:54.421
-[smooth jazz music playing]
-[bell dings]

00:03:54.465 --> 00:03:57.729
Chaz, the Smooth Jazz Troll.

00:03:57.773 --> 00:03:59.905
-["Mi Gente" playing]
-The Reggaeton Trolls.

00:03:59.949 --> 00:04:01.994
-["Russian Roulette" playing]
-♪ La, la-la-la...

00:04:02.038 --> 00:04:04.127
BARB:
The K-Pop Gang.

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:06.564
-["Hocus Pocus" playing,
singer yodeling] -And...

00:04:06.607 --> 00:04:08.131
the Yodelers.

00:04:08.174 --> 00:04:09.132
Okay.

00:04:09.175 --> 00:04:10.742
As you probably know,

00:04:10.786 --> 00:04:13.832
I'm bringing a tidal wave of
rock across this land of ours.

00:04:13.876 --> 00:04:15.791
♪

00:04:15.834 --> 00:04:18.097
And soon there will be
nothing but hard rock

00:04:18.141 --> 00:04:19.925
as far as the ear can hear.

00:04:19.969 --> 00:04:23.015
Whoever brings me Queen Poppy
gets to keep

00:04:23.059 --> 00:04:27.019
their very own music
in their very own territory.

00:04:27.063 --> 00:04:29.543
Right over here.

00:04:29.587 --> 00:04:30.849
-[Trolls murmuring, groaning]
-TROLL: Oh.

00:04:30.893 --> 00:04:32.590
I don't know.
It looks pretty tiny.

00:04:32.633 --> 00:04:33.983
You want it or not?

00:04:35.462 --> 00:04:38.509
All you have to do is
get me Queen Poppy!

00:04:38.552 --> 00:04:40.337
-Oh, okay. -Sounds like
a pretty good deal.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.773
Do you validate parking?

00:04:41.817 --> 00:04:43.644
Dude, where are the Yodelers?

00:04:43.688 --> 00:04:45.646
I heard a rumor, uh,
that they yodeled so hard,

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:47.344
an avalanche fell on 'em.

00:04:48.432 --> 00:04:50.086
Or something.

00:04:50.129 --> 00:04:52.436
Well, I don't pay you to hear.

00:04:52.479 --> 00:04:54.960
Actually, I'm doing this
for college credit.

00:04:55.004 --> 00:04:59.008
If anyone can find me
Queen Poppy and her string,

00:04:59.051 --> 00:05:01.184
-it's the Yodelers.
-♪ Just wanna have fun...

00:05:01.227 --> 00:05:02.751
[music distorts, stops]

00:05:06.058 --> 00:05:08.539
This must be where
the Country Music Trolls live.

00:05:08.582 --> 00:05:09.845
Well, it looks like
nobody's here.

00:05:09.888 --> 00:05:11.498
We're too late.
Time to go home.

00:05:11.542 --> 00:05:12.673
Come on, guys, let's go.

00:05:12.717 --> 00:05:15.807
There is no "I quit" in "team."

00:05:19.071 --> 00:05:21.813
Cock-a-doodle--

00:05:21.857 --> 00:05:24.120
Ah, never mind.

00:05:24.163 --> 00:05:26.557
[solemn country music playing]

00:05:27.384 --> 00:05:28.820
[bell chimes]

00:05:31.867 --> 00:05:34.695
♪ We don't hope for

00:05:34.739 --> 00:05:37.611
♪ Making things better

00:05:38.438 --> 00:05:41.615
♪ All we want is to

00:05:41.659 --> 00:05:44.836
♪ Keep it together

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:46.969
-[giggles]
-♪ Every day is a rainy day

00:05:47.012 --> 00:05:48.971
-Happy birthday, honey.
-♪ No change in the weather

00:05:49.014 --> 00:05:50.886
-Time to get to work.
-[yak breathing noisily]

00:05:50.929 --> 00:05:52.104
Okay, Daddy.

00:05:52.148 --> 00:05:53.453
-♪ This kind of life
-[milk spraying]

00:05:53.497 --> 00:05:55.716
-♪ Has made our hearts
-[children laughing]

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:57.588
-♪ As hard as leather
-Get it.

00:05:57.631 --> 00:05:59.633
[playful chatter]

00:05:59.677 --> 00:06:00.896
-[tumbleweed yelling]
-[children screaming]

00:06:00.939 --> 00:06:03.202
♪ And all these tears
are from ♪

00:06:03.246 --> 00:06:07.076
♪ The dust in our eyes

00:06:07.119 --> 00:06:08.860
-[Troll crying]
-♪ And all these years

00:06:08.904 --> 00:06:10.601
-[tear crying]
-♪ Just keep on

00:06:10.644 --> 00:06:13.952
♪ Passing us by

00:06:13.996 --> 00:06:17.086
♪ We all know that we're just

00:06:17.129 --> 00:06:21.003
-♪ Born to die
-[yaks mooing]

00:06:21.046 --> 00:06:24.180
♪ That's the way it goes
when you're just ♪

00:06:24.223 --> 00:06:27.096
♪ Born to die

00:06:27.139 --> 00:06:30.055
This song is so sad.

00:06:30.099 --> 00:06:32.231
Yeah, it is sad.

00:06:32.275 --> 00:06:37.106
But life is sad sometimes,
so I kind of like it.

00:06:37.149 --> 00:06:39.543
You do? Huh.

00:06:39.586 --> 00:06:41.588
But it's so different.

00:06:41.632 --> 00:06:42.981
Oh, they must not know

00:06:43.025 --> 00:06:45.331
that music's
supposed to make you happy.

00:06:45.375 --> 00:06:47.638
[gasps] That's awful.

00:06:48.813 --> 00:06:51.860
♪ And all these years
just keep on ♪

00:06:51.903 --> 00:06:55.080
♪ Passing us by

00:06:55.124 --> 00:06:57.778
-[Trolls grunting, arguing]
-♪ And all this misery

00:06:57.822 --> 00:07:01.608
♪ Makes it hard to deny

00:07:01.652 --> 00:07:03.828
-[grunting]
-♪ That's the way it goes

00:07:03.872 --> 00:07:05.438
♪ When you're just

00:07:05.482 --> 00:07:09.660
♪ Born to die.

